#! ia 1.0

@contract ia-method
  version "0.2.0"
  meaning
    says "What the IA methodology kit guarantees mechanically, one requirement per promise a check can observe. The ia plugin's reports evaluate each requirement over a workspace's work records, as advisory reports that block nothing; each case names the test that exercises it. The principles, conventions, playbooks and capabilities are guidance an agent applies, and no requirement here covers them."
    answers "What does the methodology kit guarantee, and how is each guarantee checked?"
  invariants
    REQ-METHOD-01 "The ceiling report places each task by the longest chain of required tasks between it and a provisional foundation (a cited spec that is not accepted, a required decision with no choice, or a decision with no choice that grounds a cited spec): first layer when it rests on one directly and on no task that rests on one, beyond the ceiling when any task it requires rests on one, and unknown when a record it depends on cannot be read. It names every provisional foundation the task waits on. Checking a task exits 1 beyond the ceiling and 2 when unknown (law method-provisional-foundation-ceiling)."
    REQ-METHOD-02 "A task whose status is closed is evidenced when an observation names it (as its evidence subject, or through the task's exit-evidence field) with verdict success at the task's current revision and no current refusal on the same revision: a refusal outweighs a success, a success at another revision reads stale, an inconclusive or absent verdict reads no evidence, and a record that cannot be read reads unknown, never evidenced. Every closed task with none of these is a finding, whatever the report's exit status. An observation whose interpretation basis says there was nothing to run is listed beside the findings as the author's own declaration, which no check verifies (principle method-claims-within-evidence)."
  relationships
    governs @law method-provisional-foundation-ceiling
    cites @principle method-claims-within-evidence
    cites @agent ia-method-steward

@check ia-method-coverage
  meaning
    says "Checks that every requirement of the ia-method contract has a success case and a failure case. IA evaluates the coverage; the requirements themselves are evaluated by the plugin's ceiling and exit-evidence reports, and ia validate runs neither."
    answers "Is every ia-method requirement covered by cases?"
  check
    runs COMP-COVERAGE
    scope "The ia-method requirements and their cases."
  relationships
    enforces @contract ia-method

@case method-req-01-success
  meaning
    says "A task that requires an open decision directly is reported within the first layer, and a task with ratified foundations is reported clear."
    answers "Does the ceiling report place first-layer work correctly?"
  scenario
    kind success
    given "Work records: an open decision; a task that requires it; a made decision; a task that requires the made decision."
    request "Run the ceiling report."
    expected "The first task is within the first layer, the second is clear, and nothing is beyond the ceiling."
    evaluator "plugins/ia/tests/ceiling.test.mjs :: REQ-METHOD-01 success: direct dependants stay within the first layer"
  relationships
    implements @contract ia-method#REQ-METHOD-01

@case method-req-01-failure
  meaning
    says "A task that rests on a provisional foundation only through another task is reported beyond the ceiling."
    answers "Does the ceiling report catch a second layer on a provisional foundation?"
  scenario
    kind failure
    given "Work records: a draft spec; a task that cites it; a second task that requires the first task."
    request "Run the ceiling report."
    expected "The second task is beyond the ceiling, naming the draft spec and the task between them, and checking the second task alone exits non-zero."
    evaluator "plugins/ia/tests/ceiling.test.mjs :: REQ-METHOD-01 failure: a second layer is beyond the ceiling"
  relationships
    implements @contract ia-method#REQ-METHOD-01

@case method-req-02-success
  meaning
    says "A closed task with a current success observation naming it as its evidence subject is reported evidenced."
    answers "Does the exit-evidence report accept a current success?"
  scenario
    kind success
    given "Work records: a closed task; an observation whose subject is that task, with verdict success and the task's current revision."
    request "Run the exit-evidence report for the task."
    expected "The task is evidenced, naming the observation, and the report exits 0."
    evaluator "plugins/ia/tests/exit-evidence.test.mjs :: REQ-METHOD-02 success: a current success is evidenced, through evidence.subject; --task exits 0"
  relationships
    implements @contract ia-method#REQ-METHOD-02

@case method-req-02-failure
  meaning
    says "A closed task that no observation holds a verdict for is reported as a finding, and the exit status does not hide it."
    answers "Does the exit-evidence report catch a closed task with no evidence?"
  scenario
    kind failure
    given "Work records: a closed task and no observation that names it."
    request "Run the exit-evidence report."
    expected "The first line says NO EVIDENCE for the task, and the report still exits 0, so the position and not the exit status is what to read."
    evaluator "plugins/ia/tests/exit-evidence.test.mjs :: REQ-METHOD-02 failure: a closed task with no observation is a finding, and exit 0 does not hide it: the first line says NO EVIDENCE"
  relationships
    implements @contract ia-method#REQ-METHOD-02
